id: pmc-no-empty-unreleased-337
title: Verify and complete empty Unreleased suppression for issue 337
description: "Track issue 337: include-empty retains versioned release sections only; never render an empty Unreleased section in replace, prepend, stdout, or check. Verify real pending-write, commit, tag, post-tag-check sequences and retain nonempty notes. Related earlier work: pmc-stable-itemless-check; this item owns the exact issue 337 regression proof and remaining mode gaps."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-changelog#337"
created_at: "2026-11-10T23:00:03.696Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-11T00:12:17.693Z"
assignee: codex-changelog337
claim_principal: codex-changelog337
author: codex-changelog337
comments[17]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-10T23:00:05.874Z",codex-changelog337,"Orientation counts: context reports 216 total items, 13 active (10 open, 3 in_progress), 200 closed, 3 canceled; returned focus 10 with omissions. Open list returned all 10 open items. Exact issue tag search returned 0; keyword searches returned 10 of 65 and 10 of 58. Earlier issue 333 already merged the core visibility filter and documented the policy. This item tracks issue 337 specifically and will verify actual CLI publication sequences plus stale prepend input, without weakening existing tests."
  "2026-11-10T23:01:04.309Z",codex-changelog337,"Confirmed remaining runtime gap: prepend merges keep a legacy empty Unreleased placeholder when the versioned release already exists, and also when no releases are generated. Plan: remove only whitespace-only or literal No changes. pending bodies while merging; preserve meaningful pending prose/dependencies. Keep the merged issue 333 generation filter. Add real-Git writer/commit/tag/check cases for empty, Dependabot-only and released-item windows with both include-empty settings; add per-mode migration and later-item guards. No existing test asserting an empty block needs changing."
  "2026-11-10T23:04:45.793Z",codex-changelog337,"Implementation retains the existing generation filter and cleans legacy empty pending blocks during prepend merge, including the no-generated-release case. Added nine regression tests with real Git publication fixtures and source CLI subprocesses. Initial new-fixture runs exposed expected category naming and the separate requested-release extraction guard; fixtures now retain a real released item in later-work controls so both include-empty settings exercise nonempty Unreleased rather than unrelated missing-release refusals. Existing tests remain unchanged. Typecheck, test compilation, build and docstring lint passed; docstring lint read 47 files and 268 declarations. Linked runner was retried with its supported default schema context after none/source context was refused."
  "2026-11-10T23:06:35.200Z",codex-changelog337,"Linked regression command passed 9/9 with zero failed/skipped in 88.8 seconds via pm test --run --progress. Test-result-tracking is disabled in repository settings, so this comment preserves the receipt without changing policy. npm run changelog:full regenerated CHANGELOG.md and npm run changelog:check passed, including item links. Final docstring lint read 48 files and 268 declarations. Regression tests exercise both include-empty settings, read-only checks, pre-tag/post-tag byte identity, three output modes, legacy migration, later items and later dependency entries."
  "2026-11-10T23:11:09.357Z",codex-changelog337,"Revert proof so far: timeout 1200 node scripts/prove-empty-unreleased-revert.ts runs only in a disposable copy. Baseline passed 9/9. Restoring the pre-issue-333 include-empty visibility branch failed 8/9: all three publication windows, replace/prepend/stdout tagged-HEAD checks, later-item and later-dependency guards. Reverting this PR prepend cleanup failed 2/9: prepend migration and normalized/empty-only cleanup. Dropping nonempty Unreleased failed both later-work guards (2/9). Dropping dependency-only sections failed Dependabot publication and later-dependency preservation (2/9). This distinguishes the already-merged generation fix from this PR remaining prepend fix. Final restored run is pending."
  "2026-11-10T23:12:37.029Z",codex-changelog337,"Completed revert proof: timeout 1200 node scripts/prove-empty-unreleased-revert.ts exited 0. Baseline 9/9 passed; restore-empty-Unreleased-visibility failed 8, revert-prepend-cleanup failed 2, drop-nonempty-Unreleased failed 2, drop-dependency-only-sections failed 2; final restored run passed 9/9. All failures were assertion failures in the expected named regression tests. Across the new file, eight test cases use eleven real temporary Git repositories and twenty-two real release tags; the ninth tests normalized legacy headings and no-generated-release cleanup. No existing tests changed. Documentation and regenerated changelog explicitly note callers lose the empty block on their next regeneration."
  "2026-11-10T23:17:14.166Z",codex-changelog337,"First bounded changelog/importer batch passed 742/742 tests, 41 suites, zero failed/skipped/canceled, in 611.6 seconds. Static import graph found 37 affected test files, all covered across 41 actual files in the two batches; worker-based generator parser stress tests were added separately because the worker is launched dynamically. Fresh npm run build left committed dist byte-identical. Identity/privacy audit passed 4/4 after the implementation commit. Author email audit prints only the required approved address. Second batch and full npm test gate remain pending."
  "2026-11-10T23:23:22.240Z",codex-changelog337,"Parser stress gate passed 11/11, zero failed/skipped, in 9.5 seconds. The 37 statically affected test files are covered in the two bounded commands, with 41 actual files total plus the dynamically launched parser-worker suite. Full timeout 2700 npm test is queued after the remaining importer batch. No source or dist changes have been made since implementation commit ada22de."
  "2026-11-10T23:27:49.389Z",codex-changelog337,"Second bounded importer batch hit timeout 1200 (exit 124). Report: 155 tests, 154 passed, zero assertion failures, one canceled, zero skipped, duration 1199.9 seconds. Cancellation was the existing test/release-lifecycles.test.ts native 500-lifecycle suite, still pending at the aggregate cap. This is incomplete validation, not a passing gate. All other selected files completed. The automatic full-gate prerequisite correctly refused to label the timed-out batch passed; timeout 2700 npm test was then started directly under the requested full-suite budget. No test or timeout was weakened."
  "2026-11-10T23:28:22.339Z",codex-changelog337,"Out-of-scope lifecycle validation runtime is tracked by pmc-lifecycle-test-budget, left open and unclaimed. Exact path search returned one existing closed feature (pmc-release-corrections), which tracks shipped correction semantics rather than this validation-budget concern. The current fix does not alter those tests."
  "2026-11-10T23:36:20.278Z",codex-changelog337,"Opened https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/338 at implementation commit ada22def723b2b62c1ae6b3fc9d9b8d5417b0dc4 so hosted CI can run while the local full gate continues. PR title matches the brief and body links this item on main, explains fleet release/Dependabot impact and next-regeneration removal, and explicitly records the incomplete bounded batch plus pending full result. Published body was read back and matches the prepared public-safe text. Claim remains held until local work and the final tracker receipt are complete."
  "2026-11-10T23:48:47.929Z",codex-changelog337,"Full gate completed: timeout 2700 npm test exited 0. Node test report: 1050 tests, 50 suites, 1050 passed, zero failed/canceled/skipped/todo, duration 1181.6 seconds. Existing 500-native-lifecycle stress case passed in 908.3 seconds. This full run includes all nine new regressions and every importer test; runtime source and dist remain identical to implementation commit ada22def723b2b62c1ae6b3fc9d9b8d5417b0dc4. The earlier aggregate 1200-second batch remains recorded as incomplete, not relabeled passed. PR 338 validation text is updated with these results; automated reviewer summaries are preserved. Context read: 218 total items, 15 active (11 open, 4 in_progress), 200 closed, 3 canceled; focus returned 10 with explicit omissions. No separate lint script exists; docstring lint and whitespace checks passed. Open risk: hosted checks are independent and will rerun on the final tracker commit."
  "2026-11-11T00:03:31.973Z",codex-changelog337,"Continuation for PR 338: all three review findings are valid. General rules: recognize Markdown structure only outside code blocks, and preserve meaningful whitespace in retained Markdown. Audit every heading parser and retained-slice rewrite across shared SDK, CLI, extension and output paths; add adversarial regressions and independent revert proofs. Existing branch matches the remote and includes origin/main; reuse this item and PR."
  "2026-11-11T00:07:46.680Z",codex-changelog337,"Class audit: all six shared heading-scanner consumers now ignore backtick and tilde fences, including opening length, indentation, closing-length/type rules, and unclosed fences. Found and fixed the separate committed-release receipt scanner: a fenced heading must not authorize dependency-only output. Replaced retained-slice whitespace trimming in cleanup, title creation, insertion, replacement and final merge normalization with linear blank-line trimming that preserves indentation and hard-break spaces. JSON/document/summary selection does not merge retained Markdown; the receipt regression checks those projections too. The release-date verifier reads only its own default-title generated output; other source trims normalize metadata or intentionally rebuild generated content."
  "2026-11-11T00:09:13.716Z",codex-changelog337,"Revert proof: timeout 1200 node scripts/prove-markdown-retention-revert.ts passed. Fixed baseline and restored runs: 4/4. Independent behavioral mutants fail via assertions: ignore code fences 3 tests; restore fenced publication receipts 1; trim cleanup slices 2; trim title insertion 2; trim after-title content 1; trim retained boundaries 2; trim final content line 2. The first two review findings share the fence-boundary rule; the whitespace finding is proven independently across every retained-slice operation. No existing tests were modified or removed."
  "2026-11-11T00:09:52.331Z",codex-changelog337,"Focused gate passed: timeout 1200 node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/generator.test.ts test/generator-coverage.test.ts test/generator-redos.test.ts test/markdown-retention.test.ts test/empty-unreleased.test.ts test/dependency-updates.test.ts: 274/274 tests, 31 suites, zero failures/cancellations/skips, 54.4 seconds. Packed acceptance passed 18 checks per installer (npm and Bun), 36 total, using one archive through Node/Bun SDK, standalone CLI, hosted JSON/TOON write/check and JSON generation in non-Git trackers. Archive SHA512 e2d2cdbaa8ec585f6c5fc8c03dc51271800ba764ecd266f31a4e02e621db51304230a941699e10a9831a3adde594835371990810d210ff6c192dd0d7ed7906ad. Typecheck, test compilation, docstring lint and whitespace checks passed."
  "2026-11-11T00:12:17.693Z",codex-changelog337,"Full-gate runner correction: npm appends forwarded flags after the test-file glob; process inspection showed more than two workers despite the trailing concurrency flag. Stopped the owned run (exit 143, not a passing result). The package npm test script now places --test-concurrency=2 before the file glob, so both npm and Bun callers get the requested bound without changing assertions, test selection or timeouts. Restart the full timeout 2700 npm test gate using that script."
